---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DesktopPreview from '../components/DesktopPreview.astro';
import CurrentViews from '../components/CurrentViews.astro';
import { href, site } from '../data/site';
---

<Layout>
  <section class="hero wrap refreshed-hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">
      <span class="status-dot"></span> AN ORIGINAL RUST DESKTOP OS
    </div>
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1>
        Build the system.
        <br />
        <span>Keep your place.</span>
      </h1>
      <div class="hero-aside">
        <p>
          A system that evolves.
          <br />
          Work that stays with you.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          The original kernel boots. Hosted UI continuity works. Bringing them together in the guest
          is next.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button" href={href('progress/')}>
        See current progress <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={href('concepts/')}>
        Explore the concept <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <span class="hero-review micro">Reviewed {site.reviewed}</span>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-stage">
      <figcaption class="stage-label">
        <span>THE CONTINUOUS WORKSPACE</span>
        <span>Browser concept · simulated</span>
      </figcaption>
      <DesktopPreview />
    </figure>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap reality-section" aria-labelledby="reality-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">01 / WHERE THE WORK STANDS</span>
        <h2 id="reality-title">
          Three views.
          <br />
          <span class="mint">One direction.</span>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p class="muted">
        A booting kernel, a hosted UI and an imagined desktop each tell a different part of the
        story. Here is where each runs today.
      </p>
    </div>
    <CurrentViews />
    <p class="review-note">
      M1 and M2 are locally accepted within their declared experimental and hosted scope. Review is
      implementation/self-review, not independent approval or a desktop release.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap continuity-editorial section-space">
    <div>
      <span class="section-label">02 / CONTINUITY, MADE CONCRETE</span>
      <h2>
        Change the surface.
        <br />
        <span class="mint">Keep the thought.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="large-copy">
        In the hosted UI, supported theme and layout changes preserve the document, selection,
        history, focus and window geometry.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        That is a real host result. The next challenge is to establish isolated execution, bring the
        UI into the guest, and prove continuity without resetting kernel boot identity or uptime.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={href('progress/#m3')}>
        Follow the next boundary <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div
      class="continuity-study"
      role="group"
      aria-label="Hosted resource reload: same process and window, preserved document state"
    >
      <span class="micro">HOSTED RESOURCE CONTINUITY / DEMONSTRATED</span>
      <div class="study-document">
        <span class="micro">FIELD NOTES · UNSAVED</span>
        <h3>
          A little room
          <br />
          to keep thinking.
        </h3>
        <p>
          The same document.
          <br />A new appearance.
        </p>
        <span class="study-selection">Keep this thought.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="study-transfer">
        <span>Theme + layout change</span>
        <b aria-hidden="true">↓</b>
        <span>Same process · same window</span>
      </div>
      <p class="study-caption">
        An explanatory diagram of the hosted result. Guest resource reload and app behavior
        replacement are future gates.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap principles refreshed-principles">
    <article>
      <span class="index">01 / ORIGINAL FOUNDATION</span>
      <h3>
        Own the system.
        <br />
        Make boundaries explicit.
      </h3>
      <p>
        An original Rust kernel and versioned interfaces. Every integration earns its place through
        evidence.
      </p>
      <a href={href('architecture/')}>Explore the architecture ↗</a>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="index lavender">02 / CONSIDERED EXPERIENCE</span>
      <h3>
        Good design belongs
        <br />
        in the experiment.
      </h3>
      <p>
        Keyboard access, readable text and purposeful motion are part of the hosted work. Guest
        accessibility needs its own acceptance.
      </p>
      <a href={href('concepts/')}>Try the browser simulation ↗</a>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="index copper">03 / MEASURED AMBITION</span>
      <h3>
        Less idle work.
        <br />
        Honest limits.
      </h3>
      <p>
        Hosted rendering has improved; frame-budget misses remain. The 256 MiB guest cold-idle
        target is still unmet.
      </p>
      <a href={href('progress/#performance')}>Read the hosted observations ↗</a>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap closing section-space">
    <span class="micro">A WORKING SYSTEM IS EARNED, ONE GATE AT A TIME.</span>
    <h2>
      A real beginning.
      <br />
      <span class="mint">A clear horizon.</span>
    </h2>
    <a class="button outline" href={href('progress/#roadmap')}>
      See the roadmap <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</Layout>
